[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Device and schematic object requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-R
TITLE: Resistor
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide resistor support with two terminals, resistance, scale, temperature terms and optional model binding.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check DC current and temperature scaling.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-C
TITLE: Capacitor
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide capacitor support with two terminals, capacitance, initial voltage and model parameters where supported.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check charge, AC susceptance and RC startup.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-CPOL
TITLE: Polarized capacitor
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide polarized capacitor support with explicit polarity, capacitance and optional model binding.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The forward ideal-capacitance RC profile is implemented. Positive goes to the measured node and negative goes to reference. Reverse placement is rejected by that profile before solving. Model binding and model-specific reverse behavior remain open. Verify the bounded implementation through CatalogTests and the browser and MCP native smoke tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-L
TITLE: Inductor
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide inductor support with two terminals, inductance and initial current.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check AC reactance and RL decay with nonzero initial current.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-LSAT
TITLE: Saturable inductor
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide saturable inductor support with winding terminals, nonlinear flux curve and initial state.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check differential inductance below and above saturation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-POT
TITLE: Potentiometer
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide potentiometer support with end terminals, wiper, total resistance and normalized position.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check both ends and midpoint under load.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-MEM
TITLE: Memristor
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide memristor support with two terminals, selected state law and initial state.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check state dependence and bounded transient trajectory.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-D
TITLE: Diode
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide diode support with anode, cathode, model identity and instance scaling.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare forward/reverse DC and junction charge when advertised.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-DZ
TITLE: Zener diode
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide zener diode support with anode, cathode and a model with reverse breakdown.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check reverse knee and forward conduction.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-DS
TITLE: Schottky diode
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide schottky diode support with anode, cathode and an appropriate model binding.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check forward bias and leakage against reference.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-LED
TITLE: Light-emitting diode
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide light-emitting diode support with anode, cathode and a named LED model.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check current and forward voltage for the selected card.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-XTAL
TITLE: Crystal
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide crystal support with two terminals and motional and shunt parameters.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare series and parallel resonances.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-VAR
TITLE: Varistor
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide varistor support with two terminals and a nonlinear clamping characteristic.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check both polarities and the specified knee.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-FUSE
TITLE: Fuse
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide fuse support with two terminals and an explicit trip and state model.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check overcurrent transition and post-trip resistance.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-RELAY
TITLE: Relay
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide relay support with coil terminals, contact terminals and a switching model.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check pickup, dropout and contact state.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-OPTO
TITLE: Optocoupler
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide optocoupler support with input diode terminals, output terminals and transfer model.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check isolation and transfer at multiple input currents.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-DIAC
TITLE: DIAC
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide diac support with two terminals and bidirectional breakover.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check positive and negative trigger voltages.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-SCR
TITLE: SCR
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide scr support with anode, cathode and gate.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check triggering, latching and turn-off.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-TRIAC
TITLE: TRIAC
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide triac support with two main terminals and gate.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check conduction and trigger in both polarities.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-IGBT
TITLE: IGBT
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide igbt support with collector, gate, emitter and model-specific extra terminals.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare DC transfer and switching only for qualified profiles.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-OPI
TITLE: Ideal amplifier
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide ideal amplifier support with noninverting input, inverting input and output with explicit reference and gain.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check closed-loop gain and output reference.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-OP
TITLE: Powered op amp
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide powered op amp support with noninverting and inverting inputs, both supply rails, and output.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify terminal order and output clipping when modeled.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-CMP
TITLE: Comparator
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide comparator support with differential inputs, output and supply connections when modeled.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify switching threshold and polarity.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-OTA
TITLE: Transconductance amplifier
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide transconductance amplifier support with differential inputs and explicit output terminals with a transconductance model.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare output current with the differential input.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-XFMR
TITLE: Transformer
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide transformer support with two ordered winding pairs and dot polarity.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify voltage ratio and sign.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-K
TITLE: Mutual coupling
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide mutual coupling support with two named inductors and a valid coupling coefficient.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify induced voltage and reject a missing winding.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-CORE
TITLE: Magnetic core
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide magnetic core support with magnetic terminals and explicit flux or reluctance law.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify orientation and flux response.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-T
TITLE: Lossless transmission line
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide lossless transmission line support with two ordered terminal pairs, impedance and delay.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify propagation delay and reflected pulse.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-O
TITLE: Lossy transmission line
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide lossy transmission line support with two ordered terminal pairs and a supported distributed model.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify attenuation and phase against a reference.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-CPL
TITLE: Coupled transmission line
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide coupled transmission line support with ordered near/far conductors, returns and coupling model.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify near-end and far-end crosstalk.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-RF
TITLE: RF port
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide rf port support with signal, return, port index and reference impedance.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify matched-port reflection and port ordering.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-STB
TITLE: Loop probe
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide loop probe support with two ordered series terminals and analysis binding.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify insertion preserves DC bias and identifies the loop measurement.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-PORT
TITLE: Cell interface port
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide cell interface port support with an explicit name, direction, terminal order and scope.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check emitted subcircuit ordering and duplicate-name rejection.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-GROUND
TITLE: Ground and reference symbols
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide ground and reference symbols support with reference-node identity with standard, earth and chassis artwork variants.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check distinct artwork retains the declared electrical identity.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-RAIL
TITLE: Global supply labels
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide global supply labels support with named rails including VDD, VSS, VCC and VEE with explicit scope.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check that equal labels join and unequal labels remain separate.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-CELL
TITLE: Reusable cell instance
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide reusable cell instance support with a named cell definition and its ordered interface terminals.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify two instances preserve separate internal nets.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-N-BJT
TITLE: N-type BJT
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a N-type BJT with collector, base and emitter, an explicit model selector and instance parameters validated against the selected model profile.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify pin order and polarity with independent bias sweeps. Verify derivatives, charge or thermal behavior for each claimed analysis.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-DEV-N-BJT4
TITLE: N-type substrate BJT
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a N-type substrate BJT with collector, base, emitter and substrate, an explicit model selector and instance parameters validated against the selected model profile.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Verify pin order and polarity with independent bias sweeps. Verify derivatives, charge or thermal behavior for each claimed analysis.
<<<

